 {"q": "Based on Experiment 1, catalase activity was greatest at approximately:", "c": ["37°C.", "10°C.", "45°C.", "55°C."], "cat": "IOD", "x": "Figure 1 peaks at 40 mL at 37°C."},
 {"q": "Based on Experiments 1 and 2, the conditions that produced the most oxygen were:", "c": ["37°C and pH 7.", "55°C and pH 11.", "10°C and pH 3.", "45°C and pH 9."], "cat": "IOD", "x": "Both experiments peak at 40 mL, at 37°C and at pH 7."},
 {"q": "In Experiment 2, how did the volume of oxygen produced change as pH increased from 7 to 11?", "c": ["It decreased.", "It increased.", "It stayed the same.", "It increased and then decreased."], "cat": "IOD", "x": "40 mL at pH 7, 28 mL at pH 9 and 7 mL at pH 11: a steady decrease."},
 {"q": "Based on Figure 1, if the experiment were repeated at 50°C, the volume of oxygen produced would most likely be between:", "c": ["9 mL and 30 mL.", "30 mL and 40 mL.", "0 mL and 6 mL.", "40 mL and 45 mL."], "cat": "EMI", "x": "50°C lies between 45°C (30 mL) and 55°C (9 mL)."},
 {"q": "What was the most likely purpose of Experiment 3?", "c": ["To show that the oxygen was produced by active catalase rather than by H₂O₂ breaking down on its own", "To find the optimum pH of catalase", "To measure how fast water boils", "To test whether temperature affects the volume of H₂O₂"], "cat": "SIN", "x": "Boiling destroys the enzyme; zero oxygen confirms that the gas in the other experiments came from catalase activity."},
